Gap: `verify`'s visitors `|_| ()` to `fors_recover` and `tree_fold` - Aeneas gives an `FnMut` closure returning `()` a mistyped `call_mut`, and `fors_recover` passes its visitor on as `&mut visit`, which is not translated
`verify` calls `fors_root` and `tree_root`, added here: `fors_recover` and `tree_fold` without the
visitor, over `keccak256::path_root` (keccak256 02), which is `path_fold` without one.
`fors_root` also builds the roots in a loop over the trees, where `fors_recover` has
`array::from_fn` with a closure that captures the visitor. `fors_recover` and `tree_fold` stay, for
the callers that watch; `fors_recover` is opaque in the extraction. Not a mechanical rewrite: the
claim is that a fold whose visitor does nothing computes what the fold with no visitor does.
Tool bugs: https://github.com/AeneasVerif/aeneas/issues/960 (the closure's `call_mut`),
https://github.com/pereq-dev/hax/issues/2405 (`&mut visit`).
Tests: tree_root_matches_tree_fold, against `tree_fold` with a counting visitor: the same root and
one call a level, on every layer, for paths of the tree's height, of one node and of none, at
leaves with both values of every bit.
fors_root_matches_fors_recover, against `fors_recover` with a counting visitor: the same key and
one call a level of every tree, at four sets of leaves that give every tree a left and a right
child at every level.
verify_matches_the_source (`std`), against `verify` copied from the source, on a real signature:
accepted; refused at the early `false`, with a bottom counter that gives no codeword; refused with
a counter or a path node changed on each layer, another message, a FORS secret changed, another
root.
mutation: `tree_root`'s leaf index `^ 1` -> tree_root_matches_tree_fold fails; `fors_root`'s first
tree skipped (`1..FORS_TREES`) -> fors_root_matches_fors_recover fails; `fors_root`'s path index
`^ 1` -> it fails; `verify` folding every layer on the bottom layer's path (`path(0)`) ->
verify_matches_the_source fails; `verify` accepting where there is no codeword (`return true`) ->
it fails; `verify`'s FORS key at index `idx ^ 1` -> it fails.

